{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788666233055986001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"imprudent-national-monkey","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"dc4c6a7f8cbdc73d02fdc4937909ce0e70fdec9c2818d68a004e6ca4ad878acd","event_uuid":"ec19f01c-1a87-4628-a839-089f415b008f","position":{"commit_sha":"8d1bdb18f41f61cd27646b2ad0059af3453c78d4","position":"1788657196395863384-ec19f01c-1a87-4628-a839-089f415b008f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"970692b3d77e944572f29f96b16bb65e0a358845ef85c0b88747c3fb68110c1c","event_uuid":"f116bb54-277b-451f-b747-96f6c609cfb8","position":{"commit_sha":"a113c9eaceac87641c17540c555e817ee54b833f","position":"1788657204636973264-f116bb54-277b-451f-b747-96f6c609cfb8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788657196395863384,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f116bb54-277b-451f-b747-96f6c609cfb8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nWhen the Gerrit edge fails a checkout, CI reports the change as **failing its tests**. A transport\nfault and a test verdict are the same signal today, so an infrastructure problem is attributed to\nthe author's code.\n\nThis was AC4 of `antihuman-beefwitted-zebra` (5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1). That ticket fixed the *cause* of\none such outage (an nginx `proxy_read_timeout` of 60s on the Gerrit block, now 600s). This ticket is\nthe **signal-quality half**: the next transport fault, from any cause, will still be mislabelled.\nSplitting it out because it is a genuinely separate deliverable in different files, and leaving it\nas an unmet AC on an otherwise-complete ticket would either block that close or be silently\ndropped.\n\n## Observed impact\n\nOn 2026-09-05, **four changes across three sessions** were mislabelled as broken by 504s at\ncheckout. The cost is not just the wasted vote — it is that an author (human or agent) reads\n`Verified -1`, opens the change, and starts debugging code that was never at fault. Two of tonight's\ndelegated investigations began exactly that way.\n\n## Mechanism (verified in tree at 1f7673cb2c53)\n\nTwo places collapse the distinction:\n\n1. **`.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:80-85`** — checkout runs through the third-party\n   `checkout-gerrit-change-action`. A 504 there fails the job like any other step.\n2. **`scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py:104-110`** — classifies outcomes as `TIMED OUT`,\n   `CANCELLED (not a test verdict)`, or `FAILED`. There is no transport/infrastructure class, so a\n   504 lands in `FAILED` and the voter casts `Verified -1`.\n\nNote the file already draws exactly this distinction for **cancellation** — \"not a test verdict\" is\nthe concept, already present and already respected by the voter. This ticket extends that existing\nseam to transport faults rather than inventing a new mechanism.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A checkout/transport failure is classified distinctly from a test failure, reusing the\n      existing \"not a test verdict\" seam in `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py` rather than adding a\n      parallel detection mechanism.\n- [ ] AC2 On a transport failure the bot casts **no `Verified` vote** (leaving the change at 0,\n      awaiting a real verdict) rather than `-1`. Justification: `-1` asserts the change is broken,\n      which is a claim CI cannot support when it never ran the tests. The comment must say plainly\n      that CI could not obtain the source and that this is not a statement about the change.\n- [ ] AC3 The classifier is proven by a test that feeds it a real captured 504 checkout failure and\n      asserts the transport class, plus a companion test feeding a genuine test failure and\n      asserting it still classifies as `FAILED` and still votes `-1`. Both directions, so the fix\n      cannot silently swallow real failures — that is the dangerous failure mode here, and it is\n      strictly worse than the bug being fixed.\n- [ ] AC4 A transport failure is **visible**, not silent: it is reported in the run summary and\n      distinguishable at a glance, so a stalled change is not mistaken for one nobody has voted on\n      yet.\n- [ ] AC5 The detection does not depend on a specific CI provider's proprietary signal — it keys on\n      the observable failure (HTTP status / git transport error text) so it remains portable to a\n      different provider or none, per the blocking `project.portability` criterion.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\nRetry-on-transport-failure. A retry is a *different* decision with its own risks (it can mask a\ndegrading edge and burn runner minutes), and conflating it with correct classification is how the\nscope of this ticket would quietly triple. Classification first; any retry policy is a separate\nticket that can build on the class this one introduces.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. A flaky test is a bug to root-cause, never a retry;\n`recheck` only for a provably environmental fault, stating that reasoning. `timeout` does not exist\non this macOS host (it exits 127, a silent no-op) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Do\nnot touch the shared main checkout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7c9b-3afe-5a6f-4254","ticket_type":"bug","title":"CI votes Verified -1 on transport failures, mislabelling infrastructure faults as broken changes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ec19f01c-1a87-4628-a839-089f415b008f","f116bb54-277b-451f-b747-96f6c609cfb8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788666233055986001,"uuid":"0010a803-c52f-49b8-831b-51ab9252b522"}